---
// TERMS OF USE — a plain-language draft written alongside the engineering. Have it reviewed by a lawyer before launch
// (governing law, liability limits and the operator's legal name are deliberately left for that review), and set
// PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const contact = (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL as string | undefined) || "support@bullorbear.in";
const updated = "27 October 2026";
---

<Layout title="Terms — Clipbench" description="The rules for using Clipbench and its free cloud AI credits.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 text-body leading-relaxed sm:px-6 [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:text-h3 [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_li]:mt-1 [&_p]:mt-3 [&_ul]:mt-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6">
    <h1 class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-body-sm text-(--color-text-muted)">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>Clipbench is a free video and audio editor. Editing runs in your browser. Optional cloud AI features run on our servers and use <b>free daily credits</b>. Credits have no cash value, can't be bought, sold or transferred, reset every day at 00:00 UTC, and don't carry over. We may change the credit amounts, the features, or the daily site-wide budget. If the budget is used up, cloud features pause until the next day.</p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You keep all rights to what you create and upload.</li>
      <li>By running a cloud feature, you let us and our providers process what you send, only to produce that result (see <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy</a>).</li>
      <li>You must have the rights to what you upload, and to the voices and faces in it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>You must be <b>18 or older</b> to create an account or use cloud AI features. Editing on your device has no age requirement.</p>

    <h2>Voice cloning, dubbing and lip sync</h2>
    <p>Only use a voice or likeness that is <b>yours, or that you have clear permission to use</b>. You confirm this each time. Don't use these features to impersonate anyone, to mislead people about what someone said or did, or for fraud.</p>

    <h2>AI-generated content is labelled</h2>
    <p>Audio, images and video generated or altered by our cloud AI features carry a visible label and provenance information in the file, as Indian law requires. <b>Don't remove or hide them</b>, and don't present AI-generated content as real.</p>

    <h2>Not allowed</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Anything illegal, including infringing copyright. For example, don't remove other people's watermarks or logos from their work.</li>
      <li>Sexual content involving minors, or sexual or intimate imagery of real people without their consent.</li>
      <li>Harassment, threats, hate, or content that encourages violence.</li>
      <li>Deceptive political content, or impersonating real people or organizations.</li>
      <li>Abusing the free credits, for example by automating requests, using many accounts, or reselling access, or trying to break or overload the service.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may block requests, remove content from our servers, or close accounts that break these rules.</p>

    <h2>AI results</h2>
    <p>AI output can be wrong, biased or unexpected. Check results before you publish them; you're responsible for what you publish.</p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>Clipbench is provided as-is, for free, without guarantees of availability or fitness for a particular purpose. Keep your own copies of important work: projects live in your browser and can be lost if browser data is cleared.</p>

    <h2>Open-source components</h2>
    <p>Clipbench uses open-source software and models under their own licenses; see <a href="/licenses" class="underline">Licenses</a>.</p>

    <h2>Reporting content and grievances</h2>
    <p>To report unlawful or harmful content made with Clipbench, misuse of your voice or likeness, or any other complaint, write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="underline">{contact}</a>. We'll acknowledge it within 24 hours. Content that a court or the government flags as unlawful is acted on within the time the law requires.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms; the date above shows the latest version. If a change matters, we'll say so on the site.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
